1728
01:04:08,600 --> 01:04:09,760
I have you here in this city, too.

1729
01:04:12,120 --> 01:04:13,360
That line...

1730
01:04:13,680 --> 01:04:15,280
Sun Bohan, you better hold it together.

1731
01:04:15,280 --> 01:04:16,880
Sun Bohan, don't cry.

1732
01:04:22,420 --> 01:04:24,460
(Puts the letter away)

1733
01:04:35,960 --> 01:04:36,760
He opened it again.

1734
01:04:36,760 --> 01:04:38,960
(Opens it again)
He'll definitely read it many times.

1735
01:04:49,290 --> 01:04:50,520
This letter is so romantic.

1736
01:04:50,520 --> 01:04:51,680
He must be savoring every word.

1737
01:04:51,680 --> 01:04:52,480
Exactly.

1738
01:04:53,400 --> 01:04:54,800
Writing letters like this

1739
01:04:54,800 --> 01:04:57,040
makes the longing last even longer.

1740
01:05:00,280 --> 01:05:01,600
How about we wash these together?

1741
01:05:03,760 --> 01:05:04,840
They're working.

1742
01:05:04,840 --> 01:05:06,400
How did they end up
washing dishes together?

1743
01:05:23,520 --> 01:05:25,080
(Glances over)
Washing wash.

1744
01:05:25,720 --> 01:05:27,200
Washing.

1745
01:05:27,200 --> 01:05:28,320
What's wrong with Chen Hewen?

1746
01:05:28,320 --> 01:05:29,600
Washing.

1747
01:05:29,600 --> 01:05:31,360
Why has he suddenly become so adorable?

1748
01:05:31,360 --> 01:05:32,360
There's even background music.

1749
01:05:32,360 --> 01:05:33,240
Yes.

1750
01:05:40,600 --> 01:05:41,960
This one can be washed as well.

1751
01:05:43,120 --> 01:05:43,720
Just rinse this one.

1752
01:05:43,720 --> 01:05:44,360
I don't think it was used.

1753
01:05:44,360 --> 01:05:46,160
Yeah, it probably wasn't.

1754
01:05:46,160 --> 01:05:48,240
Perhaps something was placed inside it.

1755
01:05:48,620 --> 01:05:49,720
(Leaves)
She left.

1756
01:05:49,720 --> 01:05:51,840
I feel like you two take pictures
every day.

1757
01:05:57,020 --> 01:05:58,100
(Looking)

1758
01:05:58,240 --> 01:05:59,880
I'm so sleepy today.

1759
01:06:03,320 --> 01:06:04,360
What are those two doing?

1760
01:06:04,360 --> 01:06:05,960
Washing dishes.

1761
01:06:07,520 --> 01:06:08,400
I'll take out the trash later.

1762
01:06:08,400 --> 01:06:09,080
Okay.

1763
01:06:09,760 --> 01:06:10,880
Why aren't you there?

1764
01:06:12,360 --> 01:06:13,480
Is it necessary?

1765
01:06:14,920 --> 01:06:16,320
"Is it necessary?"

1766
01:06:16,920 --> 01:06:18,040
Is it necessary?

1767
01:06:20,160 --> 01:06:20,960
All right.

1768
01:06:25,120 --> 01:06:29,160
♪I open my eyes
and see nothing but emptiness♪

1769
01:06:31,020 --> 01:06:32,620
(Removes it)

1770
01:06:34,280 --> 01:06:36,200
He's been watching her the whole time.

1771
01:06:43,860 --> 01:06:44,500
(Watching)

1772
01:06:45,200 --> 01:06:47,280
I feel like he still wants to go over
and talk to her.

1773
01:06:47,280 --> 01:06:48,240
Very much so.

1774
01:06:48,240 --> 01:06:49,800
Let's see what you two took.

1775
01:06:52,400 --> 01:06:53,160
Once this is washed,

1776
01:06:53,160 --> 01:06:54,000
we should be done.

1777
01:06:54,000 --> 01:06:54,560
All right.

1778
01:06:54,880 --> 01:06:55,960
Okay.

1779
01:06:56,200 --> 01:06:57,320
I'll leave it to you, Zhao Xilun.

1780
01:06:57,320 --> 01:06:58,480
Leave it to me.

1781
01:06:58,800 --> 01:07:00,680
How did those two get so much closer?

1782
01:07:01,330 --> 01:07:02,380
Oh, my goodness.

1783
01:07:04,800 --> 01:07:05,920
It's beautiful.

1784
01:07:06,020 --> 01:07:07,380
(Looking)
Here he comes.

1785
01:07:10,060 --> 01:07:11,480
(Looking)
I think this one looks quite good.

1786
01:07:12,360 --> 01:07:13,040
He's getting close.

1787
01:07:13,040 --> 01:07:14,160
He can start talking now.

1788
01:07:19,360 --> 01:07:20,600
These two are always...

1789
01:07:24,460 --> 01:07:27,580
(Sha Yue'er)

1790
01:07:28,000 --> 01:07:28,960
Doesn't this one look great?

1791
01:07:28,960 --> 01:07:29,860
(Loudly)

1792
01:07:32,240 --> 01:07:33,600
All right. It looks great.

1793
01:07:33,740 --> 01:07:34,540
(Looking back)

1794
01:07:36,160 --> 01:07:37,440
Cui Kaiyi doesn't feel like talking anymore.

1795
01:07:38,640 --> 01:07:39,560
A completely different vibe.

1796
01:07:40,640 --> 01:07:41,960
It is quite different.

1797
01:07:42,760 --> 01:07:44,360
They don't have much to talk about,

1798
01:07:44,360 --> 01:07:46,200
so this gets them talking.

1799
01:07:46,200 --> 01:07:46,940
Exactly.

1800
01:07:46,940 --> 01:07:48,100
(Turning)

1801
01:07:48,640 --> 01:07:49,280
Come on.

1802
01:07:49,280 --> 01:07:49,840
Who will speak

1803
01:07:49,840 --> 01:07:50,920
first?

1804
01:07:52,540 --> 01:07:54,820
(Observing)

1805
01:07:55,220 --> 01:07:56,820
(Thinking)
The colors are still slightly different.

1806
01:07:57,600 --> 01:07:58,280
Not bad.

1807
01:07:59,000 --> 01:08:00,000
Want to take a picture together?

1808
01:08:02,840 --> 01:08:03,720
Sure.

1809
01:08:03,720 --> 01:08:04,640
I'm fine either way.

1810
01:08:04,640 --> 01:08:06,160
(Proactively moving closer)
The ultimate wingwoman.

1811
01:08:06,160 --> 01:08:07,440
Cui Kaiyi, we really can count on you.

1812
01:08:07,440 --> 01:08:09,280
This place would fall apart without you.

1813
01:08:11,040 --> 01:08:12,040
Come on.

1814
01:08:12,040 --> 01:08:12,720
Let's go.

1815
01:08:12,720 --> 01:08:13,640
I'll take a picture of you two.

1816
01:08:13,640 --> 01:08:15,400
I'll take off the blanket.

1817
01:08:15,400 --> 01:08:17,280
We're pretty funny together.

1818
01:08:18,000 --> 01:08:18,480
All right.

1819
01:08:18,480 --> 01:08:19,160
Come on.

1820
01:08:22,600 --> 01:08:24,320
We're just people who love to eat.

1821
01:08:24,440 --> 01:08:25,720
Eat.

1822
01:08:29,280 --> 01:08:30,040
Beautiful.

1823
01:08:30,680 --> 01:08:31,640
Move a little closer.

1824
01:08:31,640 --> 01:08:32,160
Three,

1825
01:08:32,160 --> 01:08:32,560
two,

1826
01:08:32,560 --> 01:08:32,760
one.

1827
01:08:32,760 --> 01:08:33,320
Wait.

1828
01:08:33,800 --> 01:08:34,920
My right side looks better.

1829
01:08:35,560 --> 01:08:36,480
All right.

1830
01:08:36,840 --> 01:08:37,920
Okay, let's do it.

1831
01:08:38,360 --> 01:08:39,040
Three.

1832
01:08:39,480 --> 01:08:41,520
Some people are happy,
while others are disappointed.

1833
01:08:42,880 --> 01:08:44,240
Two.

1834
01:08:44,240 --> 01:08:45,080
Look at me.

1835
01:08:46,920 --> 01:08:48,560
Zhao Xilun seems to have ended up
in the frame.

1836
01:08:49,840 --> 01:08:50,720
It's fine.

1837
01:08:51,360 --> 01:08:52,800
Zhao Xilun is in the frame.

1838
01:08:52,800 --> 01:08:53,980
(Zhao Xilun)

1839
01:08:54,160 --> 01:08:54,840
Come here.

1840
01:08:54,840 --> 01:08:56,360
You got into the frame
while washing dishes.

1841
01:09:00,240 --> 01:09:01,040
Do I look handsome?

1842
01:09:01,560 --> 01:09:02,400
I don't know.

1843
01:09:02,400 --> 01:09:03,640
The photo hasn't been developed yet.

1844
01:09:05,640 --> 01:09:06,560
Then when will the picture

1845
01:09:06,560 --> 01:09:07,320
be developed?

1846
01:09:07,320 --> 01:09:08,720
(Photo of Sha Yue'er and Chen Hewen)

1847
01:09:08,720 --> 01:09:09,480
It hasn't developed yet.

1848
01:09:09,960 --> 01:09:10,720
It'll turn out, right?

1849
01:09:23,320 --> 01:09:24,120
May I take a look?

1850
01:09:24,120 --> 01:09:25,280
(Looking)
May I take a look?

1851
01:09:25,280 --> 01:09:26,840
Do you want to see your picture
or theirs?

1852
01:09:27,200 --> 01:09:28,080
Let me have a look.

1853
01:09:28,080 --> 01:09:29,680
(Photo of Sha Yue'er and Chen Hewen)

1854
01:09:29,680 --> 01:09:30,440
This one.

1855
01:09:30,440 --> 01:09:31,160
I just don't know

1856
01:09:31,160 --> 01:09:32,880
if it will develop properly.

1857
01:09:32,880 --> 01:09:33,520
This one...

1858
01:09:33,520 --> 01:09:35,040
This one is pretty amazing.

1859
01:09:35,920 --> 01:09:37,400
The way this one feels...

1860
01:09:37,400 --> 01:09:38,360
This one is pretty amazing.

1861
01:09:38,360 --> 01:09:39,440
It has a rather vintage feel.

1862
01:09:39,440 --> 01:09:40,480
(Moving closer)
This one is incredible.

1863
01:09:40,760 --> 01:09:41,880
These three people...

1864
01:09:43,910 --> 01:09:45,090
Wow.

1865
01:09:46,240 --> 01:09:47,040
Then our photo

1866
01:09:47,040 --> 01:09:47,760
should turn out too.

1867
01:09:49,000 --> 01:09:50,440
It should turn out, right?

1868
01:09:51,240 --> 01:09:52,120
It should.

1869
01:09:52,120 --> 01:09:53,360
It's just taking a while, right?

1870
01:09:55,120 --> 01:09:56,040
It must just be taking longer.

1871
01:09:57,540 --> 01:09:59,780
(Holding the photograph)

1872
01:09:59,880 --> 01:10:01,120
Actually, this one is quite good too.

1873
01:10:01,120 --> 01:10:02,440
All of these pictures look great.

1874
01:10:04,800 --> 01:10:05,800
Why does Chen Hewen move away

1875
01:10:05,800 --> 01:10:07,240
every time Zhao Xilun leaves?

1876
01:10:08,880 --> 01:10:10,780
Why do you keep avoiding me?

1877
01:10:10,780 --> 01:10:11,580
(Those familiar words)

1878
01:10:11,920 --> 01:10:12,520
Grab that one.

1879
01:10:12,520 --> 01:10:13,520
Why do you keep avoiding me?

1880
01:10:13,520 --> 01:10:14,440
Where am I supposed to hide?

1881
01:10:15,600 --> 01:10:17,440
He's probably just getting something.

1882
01:10:18,920 --> 01:10:19,840
My camera.

1883
01:10:22,880 --> 01:10:24,200
Have you worn this T-shirt before?

1884
01:10:24,440 --> 01:10:25,280
The shirt.

1885
01:10:26,040 --> 01:10:27,000
I have not.

1886
01:10:27,960 --> 01:10:29,840
Why am I so sleepy?

1887
01:10:30,240 --> 01:10:31,280
You didn't get enough rest?

1888
01:10:31,720 --> 01:10:32,760
I told you,

1889
01:10:32,760 --> 01:10:34,040
I actually got plenty of rest.

1890
01:10:35,280 --> 01:10:36,600
I'm like that too.

1891
01:10:44,080 --> 01:10:45,160
What is it?

1892
01:10:47,600 --> 01:10:48,920
There is still film inside.

1893
01:10:49,480 --> 01:10:51,240
(Thinking)
Come on, let's take a picture together.

1894
01:10:52,320 --> 01:10:52,760
Let me help.

1895
01:10:52,760 --> 01:10:53,160
Is that okay

1896
01:10:53,160 --> 01:10:54,720
if it takes a while to develop?

1897
01:10:55,520 --> 01:10:56,200
Let's wait.

1898
01:10:56,200 --> 01:10:57,040
Then we will wait.

1899
01:10:57,400 --> 01:10:58,720
I'll put it back up.

1900
01:10:58,720 --> 01:11:00,560
Take a picture of Liang Xiaoyu first.

1901
01:11:00,560 --> 01:11:02,400
(Liang Xiaoyu)
Let her take one by herself.

1902
01:11:02,440 --> 01:11:04,760
Meng suggested taking
a picture of the two of them,

1903
01:11:04,760 --> 01:11:06,240
and Cui Kaiyi took one of Chen Hewen
and Sha Yue'er.

1904
01:11:06,240 --> 01:11:06,960
They're all helping.

1905
01:11:07,140 --> 01:11:08,700
(Adjusting)
Okay.

1906
01:11:08,720 --> 01:11:09,760
Does the background look good?

1907
01:11:13,400 --> 01:11:14,160
I think it is fine.

1908
01:11:14,160 --> 01:11:14,680
But

1909
01:11:14,680 --> 01:11:15,680
stand a little farther away.

1910
01:11:18,680 --> 01:11:19,320
That's too far.

1911
01:11:19,680 --> 01:11:20,600
That's too far.

1912
01:11:23,360 --> 01:11:24,400
Do I need to stand this close?

1913
01:11:26,200 --> 01:11:27,040
Three.

1914
01:11:31,060 --> 01:11:31,900
(Looking)

1915
01:11:31,920 --> 01:11:32,840
Sha Yue'er turned around.

1916
01:11:32,840 --> 01:11:33,480
Oh, my goodness.

1917
01:11:33,480 --> 01:11:34,200
Sha Yue'er.

1918
01:11:35,400 --> 01:11:36,200
Two.

1919
01:11:39,560 --> 01:11:40,360
One.

1920
01:11:43,920 --> 01:11:44,440
I think

1921
01:11:44,440 --> 01:11:45,120
when he grabbed the camera,

1922
01:11:45,120 --> 01:11:46,560
he wanted to take another picture,

1923
01:11:46,560 --> 01:11:47,520
just of him and Sha Yue'er.

1924
01:11:47,800 --> 01:11:49,440
However, many things

1925
01:11:49,440 --> 01:11:50,920
happened along the way.

1926
01:11:52,320 --> 01:11:54,480
Let's wait. Could I be the lucky one?

1927
01:11:54,480 --> 01:11:55,560
I think it is possible.

1928
01:11:55,560 --> 01:11:57,080
It is blue, right?

1929
01:11:58,360 --> 01:11:59,640
The pictures turned out beautifully.

1930
01:11:59,640 --> 01:12:00,440
It looks good.

1931
01:12:00,440 --> 01:12:01,280
Yes.

1932
01:12:01,600 --> 01:12:02,760
What time did you arrive today?

1933
01:12:03,240 --> 01:12:04,360
What time did you arrive today?

1934
01:12:04,760 --> 01:12:05,560
The fourth one.

1935
01:12:12,440 --> 01:12:13,560
It's beautiful.

1936
01:12:17,830 --> 01:12:18,960
Did you go back to practice pool?

1937
01:12:19,400 --> 01:12:21,080
I don't know how to play this.

1938
01:12:21,080 --> 01:12:23,440
Didn't you make quite
a mess of it last time?

1939
01:12:24,280 --> 01:12:24,880
Play?

1940
01:12:25,280 --> 01:12:25,960
Play?

1941
01:12:26,600 --> 01:12:27,160
Let's play.

1942
01:12:27,720 --> 01:12:29,280
He's here.

1943
01:12:31,160 --> 01:12:31,800
What?

1944
01:12:31,800 --> 01:12:32,200
What is this?

1945
01:12:32,200 --> 01:12:32,680
Pool.

1946
01:12:32,960 --> 01:12:34,680
Handball.

1947
01:12:35,280 --> 01:12:36,000
But it's clear

1948
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:37,800
that Chen Hewen is trying to change.

1949
01:12:39,200 --> 01:12:40,480
So, what are you two playing?

1950
01:12:41,280 --> 01:12:42,040
Just playing

1951
01:12:42,040 --> 01:12:42,920
to relax.

1952
01:12:43,240 --> 01:12:44,160
Nothing serious.

1953
01:12:45,180 --> 01:12:46,380
(Looking)

1954
01:12:51,760 --> 01:12:52,400
We will see.

1955
01:12:52,400 --> 01:12:53,280
We just hit them.

1956
01:12:53,280 --> 01:12:54,920
We try to sink them
into the bottom pocket.

1957
01:12:54,920 --> 01:12:55,880
All right. Five balls each.

1958
01:12:55,880 --> 01:12:57,640
Whoever sinks more balls wins.
How does that sound?

1959
01:12:59,320 --> 01:13:00,120
All right.

1960
01:13:00,560 --> 01:13:01,600
The loser...

1961
01:13:03,640 --> 01:13:04,640
The loser...

1962
01:13:05,240 --> 01:13:06,480
20 push-ups...

1963
01:13:06,480 --> 01:13:07,160
No, squats.

1964
01:13:12,920 --> 01:13:13,880
All right.

1965
01:13:13,880 --> 01:13:15,480
You're really into it now.

1966
01:13:15,480 --> 01:13:16,960
I'll go first, then.

1967
01:13:16,960 --> 01:13:17,440
All right.

1968
01:13:19,100 --> 01:13:21,180
(First ball goes straight
into the pocket)

1969
01:13:21,480 --> 01:13:22,320
Wow.

1970
01:13:27,160 --> 01:13:28,280
That hand gesture...

1971
01:13:28,760 --> 01:13:29,800
What is that?

1972
01:13:30,040 --> 01:13:30,440
Men

1973
01:13:30,440 --> 01:13:30,920
become fools

1974
01:13:30,920 --> 01:13:32,120
the moment

1975
01:13:32,120 --> 01:13:33,200
(Fools)
they get competitive.

1976
01:13:37,480 --> 01:13:38,200
Honestly,

1977
01:13:38,200 --> 01:13:38,840
one is enough,

1978
01:13:38,840 --> 01:13:39,400
you know?

1979
01:13:39,400 --> 01:13:41,000
All right.

1980
01:13:41,000 --> 01:13:42,040
Second ball.

1981
01:13:42,040 --> 01:13:45,300
(Chen Hewen: One out of five)

1982
01:13:45,300 --> 01:13:50,060
(Chen Hewen: Two out of five)

1983
01:13:50,080 --> 01:13:50,720
All right.

1984
01:13:51,160 --> 01:13:51,840
He's taking it easy.

1985
01:13:52,440 --> 01:13:53,760
Come on, let me try.

1986
01:13:54,000 --> 01:13:55,000
Sha Yue'er is playing too?

1987
01:13:55,000 --> 01:13:55,400
Yes.

1988
01:13:58,400 --> 01:13:59,480
One.

1989
01:14:01,860 --> 01:14:03,260
(Looking)
Two.

1990
01:14:03,880 --> 01:14:05,200
What happened to this ball?

1991
01:14:06,060 --> 01:14:07,060
(Sha Yue'er: Zero out of five)
Three.

1992
01:14:07,180 --> 01:14:08,260
(Two balls remaining)

1993
01:14:09,580 --> 01:14:11,220
(Sha Yue'er: Zero out of five)

1994
01:14:11,320 --> 01:14:12,600
You just wouldn't blame your own hand.

1995
01:14:15,320 --> 01:14:16,200
Just nudged it in.

1996
01:14:18,620 --> 01:14:19,620
(Last ball)

1997
01:14:19,620 --> 01:14:23,180
(Sha Yue'er: Zero out of five)

1998
01:14:23,180 --> 01:14:24,960
(Sha Yue'er: One out of five)

1999
01:14:24,960 --> 01:14:25,760
She got one in.

2000
01:14:26,760 --> 01:14:27,600
I did it.

2001
01:14:41,060 --> 01:14:43,260
(Zhao Xilun: Zero out of five)

2002
01:14:44,000 --> 01:14:44,600
Okay.

2003
01:14:47,700 --> 01:14:49,060
(Zhao Xilun: Zero out of five)

2004
01:14:49,080 --> 01:14:49,980
(Same position)
Zero out of three.

2005
01:14:50,000 --> 01:14:51,560
He is deliberately hitting it
to the side.

2006
01:14:51,560 --> 01:14:52,920
It is so obvious.

2007
01:14:52,920 --> 01:14:54,640
He doesn't want Sha Yue'er
to do the punishment.

2008
01:14:55,080 --> 01:14:56,240
Why do you keep aiming there?

2009
01:14:58,840 --> 01:14:59,960
This one went in.

2010
01:14:59,960 --> 01:15:00,600
Got the feel for it?

2011
01:15:00,600 --> 01:15:01,400
Yes.

2012
01:15:01,400 --> 01:15:02,240
(Four out of four: Last ball)

2013
01:15:02,240 --> 01:15:03,100
(Two out of five)
Just hit it casually.

2014
01:15:03,360 --> 01:15:03,960
Just hit it casually.

2015
01:15:03,960 --> 01:15:05,440
(Zhao Xilun: Zero out of five,
casually tossing the ball)

2016
01:15:05,440 --> 01:15:06,260
Hit the middle pocket.

2017
01:15:06,300 --> 01:15:07,740
(Zero out of five: Loses)
It went into the bottom pocket.

2018
01:15:11,880 --> 01:15:12,480
All right.

2019
01:15:12,480 --> 01:15:14,720
You came up with the game,
only to lose in the end.

2020
01:15:14,720 --> 01:15:15,480
You...

2021
01:15:16,120 --> 01:15:17,520
What are you doing?

2022
01:15:18,900 --> 01:15:21,500
(Doing push-ups under the table)

2023
01:15:26,960 --> 01:15:28,840
You're unbelievable, Zhao Xilun.

2024
01:15:34,840 --> 01:15:35,760
They're quite different.

2025
01:15:35,760 --> 01:15:37,040
One makes it obvious when he's going

2026
01:15:37,040 --> 01:15:37,760
easy on you,

2027
01:15:37,760 --> 01:15:38,560
while the other

2028
01:15:38,560 --> 01:15:40,080
keeps it to himself.

2029
01:15:40,360 --> 01:15:42,380
Come and "buy" some bread!

2030
01:15:42,380 --> 01:15:44,180
(Liang Renfang brought everyone bread)
This one. I want this one.

2031
01:15:44,180 --> 01:15:44,760
Come over.

2032
01:15:45,280 --> 01:15:46,400
Come over.

2033
01:15:47,200 --> 01:15:48,320
I'll go get some bread.

2034
01:15:50,360 --> 01:15:51,360
Every time he goes over,

2035
01:15:51,360 --> 01:15:52,480
if he feels something

2036
01:15:52,480 --> 01:15:53,680
is holding him back,

2037
01:15:53,680 --> 01:15:54,760
he just backs off.

2038
01:15:54,880 --> 01:15:55,680
He walks away

2039
01:15:55,680 --> 01:15:57,360
because the pressure
over there is too much.

2040
01:15:57,360 --> 01:15:58,400
He instinctively moves toward

2041
01:15:58,400 --> 01:15:59,080
somewhere he feels

2042
01:15:59,080 --> 01:15:59,760
less pressure.

2043
01:15:59,760 --> 01:16:00,600
I think some people

2044
01:16:00,600 --> 01:16:02,440
feel a certain sense of embarrassment

2045
01:16:02,440 --> 01:16:03,320
when it comes

2046
01:16:03,320 --> 01:16:05,000
to competing over something.

2047
01:16:12,600 --> 01:16:13,880
You two look like you're running...

2048
01:16:13,880 --> 01:16:14,880
It's like they've opened a shop.

2049
01:16:15,360 --> 01:16:16,560
You're seriously running
a bread shop,

2050
01:16:16,560 --> 01:16:17,920
while Liang Xiaoyu is over there

2051
01:16:17,920 --> 01:16:19,040
doing her thing.

2052
01:16:19,400 --> 01:16:20,360
Would you like some bread?

2053
01:16:20,360 --> 01:16:21,680
Come and buy some.

2054
01:16:22,960 --> 01:16:24,040
How do you sell it?

2055
01:16:24,040 --> 01:16:25,720
Just pick one, and I'll pack it for you.

2056
01:16:25,920 --> 01:16:26,480
All right.

2057
01:16:27,080 --> 01:16:28,120
Then I will take the one

2058
01:16:28,680 --> 01:16:29,920
that smells particularly good.

2059
01:16:31,000 --> 01:16:32,600
And I'll have one of these as well.

2060
01:16:34,360 --> 01:16:35,080
We can order too?

2061
01:16:35,080 --> 01:16:35,720
Anything else?

2062
01:16:35,720 --> 01:16:36,720
That's enough.

2063
01:16:36,720 --> 01:16:37,400
I'll pack it for you.

2064
01:16:37,400 --> 01:16:38,080
What does that mean?

2065
01:16:38,760 --> 01:16:39,720
I'm so tired.

2066
01:16:40,280 --> 01:16:41,480
He'll stay by her side.

2067
01:16:44,960 --> 01:16:46,280
I'm actually quite tired too.

2068
01:16:46,280 --> 01:16:47,240
Let's find somewhere to sit.

2069
01:16:47,960 --> 01:16:49,000
Where would you like to go?

2070
01:16:49,000 --> 01:16:50,800
Just somewhere we can sit.

2071
01:16:50,800 --> 01:16:52,400
Sun Bohan was probably
in the study just now.

2072
01:16:55,660 --> 01:16:56,660
(Looking)

2073
01:17:03,760 --> 01:17:04,920
There are sandwiches here.

2074
01:17:04,920 --> 01:17:06,040
There is ham and egg.

2075
01:17:06,520 --> 01:17:07,360
And this one is...

2076
01:17:07,360 --> 01:17:08,320
It's delicious.

2077
01:17:08,320 --> 01:17:09,400
Yes, it's like this.

2078
01:17:09,780 --> 01:17:12,060
(Leaves)

2079
01:17:16,560 --> 01:17:18,480
Sorry. You are the real boss.

2080
01:17:19,440 --> 01:17:20,120
I'm dying of laughter.

2081
01:17:20,120 --> 01:17:22,240
I think Liang Xiaoyu will quietly tell you.

2082
01:17:22,640 --> 01:17:23,440
Tell me what?

2083
01:17:23,880 --> 01:17:24,720
It's nothing.

2084
01:17:27,840 --> 01:17:28,600
Look, he has returned

2085
01:17:28,600 --> 01:17:29,520
to the exact same spot again.

2086
01:17:29,520 --> 01:17:30,640
Yes.

2087
01:17:48,680 --> 01:17:50,000
Thank you, boss.

2088
01:17:50,000 --> 01:17:50,800
You're welcome.

2089
01:17:50,800 --> 01:17:52,320
Thank you, boss,
for giving us free bread.

2090
01:17:54,640 --> 01:17:55,880
Let's go.

2091
01:17:56,980 --> 01:17:58,500
(Looking)

2092
01:18:00,080 --> 01:18:00,880
Are you going upstairs?

2093
01:18:00,880 --> 01:18:01,320
Yes.

2094
01:18:01,320 --> 01:18:01,800
Help me carry these.

2095
01:18:01,800 --> 01:18:02,640
I'll take them up for you.

2096
01:18:02,640 --> 01:18:03,240
Thank you.

2097
01:18:03,240 --> 01:18:04,080
Give them to me.

2098
01:18:04,080 --> 01:18:05,040
I want to play pool here.

2099
01:18:05,040 --> 01:18:05,840
All right. Go ahead.

2100
01:18:07,640 --> 01:18:08,480
You're going upstairs?

2101
01:18:08,480 --> 01:18:10,040
I'll go upstairs while she plays.

2102
01:18:12,960 --> 01:18:13,800
If you're playing alone,

2103
01:18:13,800 --> 01:18:15,240
I'll head upstairs.

2104
01:18:18,000 --> 01:18:19,080
I didn't beat you last time.

2105
01:18:19,400 --> 01:18:20,080
Really?

2106
01:18:20,880 --> 01:18:21,680
Yes.

2107
01:18:22,120 --> 01:18:23,000
I don't remember that.

2108
01:18:24,800 --> 01:18:25,760
Didn't you win?

2109
01:18:27,180 --> 01:18:27,600
Yes.

2110
01:18:27,600 --> 01:18:28,480
I'll set up the balls.

2111
01:18:34,280 --> 01:18:35,360
You can play now.

2112
01:18:35,360 --> 01:18:36,600
All right. I will just
pick one and play.

2113
01:18:36,600 --> 01:18:37,480
Choose whichever one you like.

2114
01:18:41,760 --> 01:18:42,800
Could you teach me?

2115
01:18:44,000 --> 01:18:46,080
Try to keep your hand flat.

2116
01:18:46,080 --> 01:18:48,160
Your hand is hovering.

2117
01:18:48,160 --> 01:18:48,440
Flat.

2118
01:18:48,440 --> 01:18:49,240
Then do this.

2119
01:18:49,240 --> 01:18:49,880
Raise it slightly.

2120
01:18:50,500 --> 01:18:51,780
(Adjusting)

2121
01:18:52,080 --> 01:18:53,440
Then place your thumb here.

2122
01:18:55,840 --> 01:18:56,560
Go ahead.

2123
01:18:59,880 --> 01:19:00,700
Very impressive.

2124
01:19:00,700 --> 01:19:01,680
(Complimenting)
That was impressive.

2125
01:19:02,320 --> 01:19:03,880
(Laughs)
You are a good teacher.

2126
01:19:03,880 --> 01:19:04,880
Let's see which one you can hit.

2127
01:19:05,040 --> 01:19:06,120
The green one.

2128
01:19:07,720 --> 01:19:08,600
Raise your hand higher.

2129
01:19:08,600 --> 01:19:09,280
For example, look at this.

2130
01:19:09,280 --> 01:19:09,760
This is how

2131
01:19:09,760 --> 01:19:11,120
I would hit it.

2132
01:19:11,460 --> 01:19:12,760
(Moving closer)

2133
01:19:12,760 --> 01:19:14,520
I hold my cue quite high.

2134
01:19:17,880 --> 01:19:18,440
You don't need me.

2135
01:19:18,440 --> 01:19:19,960
You have already...

2136
01:19:19,960 --> 01:19:21,200
He really knows how to flatter people.

2137
01:19:27,240 --> 01:19:28,560
You are quite impressive.

2138
01:19:28,840 --> 01:19:30,000
How is she so good at everything?

2139
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:30,720
Incredibly versatile.

2140
01:19:30,720 --> 01:19:31,920
Thank you, Chen Hewen.

2141
01:19:32,720 --> 01:19:35,240
Well done.

2142
01:19:35,600 --> 01:19:36,800
Well done.

2143
01:19:37,880 --> 01:19:39,860
(Looking at photo)
What is he looking at?

2144
01:19:39,860 --> 01:19:43,300
(Photo of him and Sha Yue'er)

2145
01:19:43,920 --> 01:19:46,080
This is getting difficult.

2146
01:19:47,320 --> 01:19:48,760
He has lost interest in the game.

2147
01:19:48,760 --> 01:19:49,200
Exactly.

2148
01:19:51,440 --> 01:19:52,440
Master, give me some guidance.

2149
01:19:54,400 --> 01:19:55,240
Not in the right state.

2150
01:19:56,280 --> 01:19:58,200
This is becoming rather difficult.

2151
01:19:59,880 --> 01:20:00,880
Let me see which ball you can hit.

2152
01:20:01,520 --> 01:20:03,000
He is remarkably good
at hiding his feelings.

2153
01:20:04,280 --> 01:20:05,640
I feel that Chen Hewen

2154
01:20:05,640 --> 01:20:07,200
keeps a lot to himself.

2155
01:20:08,200 --> 01:20:09,360
I think Chen Hewen

2156
01:20:09,360 --> 01:20:11,720
would respond well
to calm and open communication.

2157
01:20:11,720 --> 01:20:12,760
Don't provoke him

2158
01:20:12,760 --> 01:20:13,480
or place emotional

2159
01:20:13,480 --> 01:20:14,740
pressure on him.

2160
01:20:14,740 --> 01:20:15,953
(Chen Hewen responds well)
He tends to avoid pressure.

2161
01:20:15,953 --> 01:20:16,640
(to gentle communication)
Yes.

2162
01:20:16,640 --> 01:20:18,080
Whenever he feels pressured,

2163
01:20:18,080 --> 01:20:19,120
he quietly pulls away.

2164
01:20:19,360 --> 01:20:20,440
When he feels that pressure,

2165
01:20:20,440 --> 01:20:21,400
he instinctively pulls away.

2166
01:20:21,400 --> 01:20:23,760
But if you speak to him calmly,

2167
01:20:23,760 --> 01:20:24,400
like Liang Xiaoyu does,

2168
01:20:24,400 --> 01:20:25,320
simply listen

2169
01:20:25,320 --> 01:20:26,040
and ask,

2170
01:20:26,040 --> 01:20:26,840
"Why? What happened?"

2171
01:20:26,840 --> 01:20:28,760
I think he would gradually

2172
01:20:28,760 --> 01:20:29,960
respond much

2173
01:20:29,960 --> 01:20:30,840
better.

2174
01:20:30,840 --> 01:20:31,760
He responds very well

2175
01:20:31,760 --> 01:20:33,200
to calm communication.

2176
01:20:33,200 --> 01:20:35,280
I think he is afraid
of conflict, so he tries

2177
01:20:35,280 --> 01:20:36,720
to consider everyone's feelings.

2178
01:20:36,720 --> 01:20:37,440
He wants the situation

2179
01:20:37,440 --> 01:20:39,640
to remain completely

2180
01:20:39,640 --> 01:20:40,760
harmonious and calm.

2181
01:20:40,760 --> 01:20:42,600
That is why he treats
Liang Xiaoyu the same way.

2182
01:20:42,600 --> 01:20:44,400
He does not want her

2183
01:20:44,400 --> 01:20:46,640
to have any negative
feelings toward him.

2184
01:20:46,640 --> 01:20:48,240
He wants to take care of everyone.

2185
01:20:48,840 --> 01:20:51,000
When someone tries too hard
to accommodate everyone,

2186
01:20:51,000 --> 01:20:53,760
(Expert, Sami)
they often end up neglecting themselves.

2187
01:20:54,200 --> 01:20:54,640
When you

2188
01:20:54,640 --> 01:20:55,720
neglect your own needs,

2189
01:20:55,720 --> 01:20:56,720
you no longer feel connected

2190
01:20:56,720 --> 01:20:58,120
to the people around you.

2191
01:20:58,520 --> 01:21:00,080
That is why, in many situations,

2192
01:21:00,080 --> 01:21:01,720
we need to take a step back

2193
01:21:01,720 --> 01:21:02,560
and observe ourselves.

2194
01:21:02,760 --> 01:21:03,240
In fact,

2195
01:21:03,240 --> 01:21:05,120
this reflects different
attachment styles.

2196
01:21:05,480 --> 01:21:06,920
Everyone's daily life

2197
01:21:06,920 --> 01:21:08,040
will be different

2198
01:21:08,040 --> 01:21:08,880
in its own way.

2199
01:21:09,120 --> 01:21:11,120
Some people avoid the situation first

2200
01:21:11,120 --> 01:21:12,080
before dealing with it.

2201
01:21:12,080 --> 01:21:12,920
Others respond

2202
01:21:12,920 --> 01:21:14,360
with aggression first, then withdraw,

2203
01:21:14,360 --> 01:21:15,080
and process it.

2204
01:21:15,080 --> 01:21:16,840
There is no right or wrong approach.

2205
01:21:16,840 --> 01:21:18,080
However, our responses may be shaped

2206
01:21:18,080 --> 01:21:19,720
by the experiences we have had

2207
01:21:20,160 --> 01:21:21,400
while growing up.

2208
01:21:23,380 --> 01:21:27,460
(Don't go anywhere. The next episode
is even more romantic.)
